格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"DSH ⇄ Cindy 手机客户端桥接插件（Host 侧）：会话/消息/审批/todo/goal 的手机通道，含实测定案与项目记忆","id":"gh:1374427473","install_available":true,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-cindy-host","slug":"chanyuenpang/dsh-cindy-host","topics":["device-link","dsh","dsh-plugin"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"DSH ⇄ Cindy 手机客户端桥接插件（Host 侧）：会话/消息/审批/todo/goal 的手机通道，含实测定案与项目记忆"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# DSH Cindy Host"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"A Host-side adapter connecting current Cindy clients to DeepSeek Harness."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"## Requirements and installation"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"Version **0.1.41** adds DSH `0.2.2-rc.1` compatibility and keeps historical ordinary forks visible b"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"y classifying subagents through `origin`, not parent lineage. It retains 0.1.40's task provenance, s"},{"id":"p5s3","text":"ystem credential storage, image delivery, thumbnails, work titles, history stability and interruptio"},{"id":"p5s4","text":"n controls. Handset re-entry, rendering and white-screen acceptance remain separate."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"It supports the exact **DSH 0.2.2-rc.1** carrier, while retaining `0.2.2-alpha.2`, `0.2.1-rc.3`, `0."},{"id":"p6s2","text":"2.1-rc.4` and `0.2.1-rc.5`. DSH 0.2.2 requires **Node.js >=24.9** (RC tested with 24.18); the older "},{"id":"p6s3","text":"carriers retain this plugin's Node.js >=22.16 minimum. Agent/session/settings peers and alpha Schema"},{"id":"p6s4","text":"stery are explicitly allowed, not a blanket promise for future prereleases. RC validation covers iso"},{"id":"p6s5","text":"lated Web installation and runtime smoke; the prior alpha checks cover core contracts. Neither estab"},{"id":"p6s6","text":"lishes relay or handset acceptance. Install through the Desktop DSH plugin manager. CLI-managed prof"},{"id":"p6s7","text":"or handset acceptance. Install through the Desktop DSH plugin manager. CLI-managed profiles can use:"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"Reload the Host plugin after installation. A full DSH restart is separate. Keep existing Cindy sign-"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"in, device identity and settings; do not run two Host processes with the same identity."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"## 0.1.41: DSH 0.2.2 RC compatibility"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"Accepts the exact RC Agent, Session and Settings SDKs, Cordis 4.1 and Schemastery 3.19. Historical o"},{"id":"p10s2","text":"rdinary forks can retain `parentSession`/`parentSessionId`; only `origin: 'subagent'` classifies del"},{"id":"p10s3","text":"egated sessions. The correction covers discovery, active reads, direct lookup and creation pushes. C"},{"id":"p10s4","text":"indy's handshake identity remains unchanged. See verification details for candidate checks and the e"},{"id":"p10s5","text":"arlier local prototype's limits."},{"id":"p11s1","text":"## 0.1.36: interruption controls"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"The existing Cindy acknowledgement/dismissal actions update owner-scoped display preferences, not fa"},{"id":"p12s2","text":"ilure or completion facts. Manual continuation is a new human input; it verifies the current native "},{"id":"p12s3","text":"tail and effective plan-mode off rather than retrying old tool calls. These changes are Host-only: C"},{"id":"p12s4","text":"indy is a read-only protocol/test dependency. See the diagnostic protocol and limitations for persis"},{"id":"p12s5","text":"tence, concurrency and current-client boundaries. Source contracts do not establish live-handset acc"},{"id":"p12s6","text":"oncurrency and current-client boundaries. Source contracts do not establish live-handset acceptance."},{"id":"p13s1","text":"## 0.1.32: credentials without keytar"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"No native npm credential module or C++ build toolchain is required. Linux uses `secret-tool` with an"},{"id":"p14s2","text":" unlocked Secret Service (headless sessions need their own DBus/keyring setup); macOS uses the syste"},{"id":"p14s3","text":"m Keychain through `/usr/bin/security`. Both keep the existing `DSH Cindy Host` service and installa"},{"id":"p14s4","text":"tion-specific account."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"Windows uses built-in Windows PowerShell/.NET DPAPI (CurrentUser), then stores **only encrypted ciph"},{"id":"p15s2","text":"ertext** in DSH’s native `credentials` record service. DSH owns the private file, atomic writes and "},{"id":"p15s3","text":"record removal; tokens never enter settings, child-process arguments or logs. No Cindy/Electron inte"},{"id":"p15s4","text":"gration is required. DSH without the record API, blocked PowerShell, a locked keychain, missing `sec"},{"id":"p15s5","text":"ret-tool`, or damaged ciphertext produces a storage error, not a missing login or a plaintext fallba"},{"id":"p15s6","text":"-tool`, or damaged ciphertext produces a storage error, not a missing login or a plaintext fallback."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"Windows users upgrading from keytar may need to sign in once through the **DSH settings card**. Old "},{"id":"p16s2","text":"Windows Credential Manager entries are not automatically read or deleted; rollback can still see the"},{"id":"p16s3","text":"m, and users can remove them manually after confirming the new login. Windows standalone `npm run lo"},{"id":"p16s4","text":"gin/logout/host` has no DSH credential context: use the settings card instead. Linux/macOS standalon"},{"id":"p16s5","text":"e commands keep using the same system keychain. Different DSH homes remain isolated. DPAPI ciphertex"},{"id":"p16s6","text":"t is not a portable backup: another OS user/machine generally cannot decrypt it."},{"id":"p17s1","text":"Native Windows persistence smoke (fake credentials and an isolated temporary DSH document only):"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"The runtime root must contain compiled DSH SDK packages under node_modules. This checks real DPAPI e"},{"id":"p19s2","text":"ncryption, native DSH atomic persistence, fresh-context restore, renewal and logout without accessin"},{"id":"p19s3","text":"g a daily profile. Linux/macOS command adapters have mock-contract tests; live keychain acceptance m"},{"id":"p19s4","text":"ust run on those operating systems."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"## 0.1.32: DSH 0.2.2-alpha.2 compatibility"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"- Accept the exact alpha session/settings carrier and `@deepseek-ai/schemastery@3.18.6-alpha.1` with"},{"id":"p21s2","text":"out installing another DSH runtime as a dependency.\n- Draft skill discovery uses `agentPresets.acqui"},{"id":"p21s3","text":"reScope()` and releases the revision after success or failure. Live Agents prefer their isolated pre"},{"id":"p21s4","text":"set skill service; older standing-key carriers retain their fallback.\n- Isolated alpha core-contract"},{"id":"p21s5","text":" smoke exercises the real compatibility evaluator, Cordis Loader, Session message folding, and prese"},{"id":"p21s6","text":"t-scoped skill discovery. It also checks controller/settings/archive method presence. This is **not*"},{"id":"p21s7","text":"* full Web/profile-persistence/relay/handset acceptance; those remain unverified on alpha. No daily "},{"id":"p21s8","text":"profile is modified or restarted."},{"id":"p22s1","text":"Reproduce without installing into a DSH profile:"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"Unpack `npm pack` output beneath that npm project's directory, so its imports use the alpha peers, t"},{"id":"p24s2","text":"hen run (the smoke asserts that resolution):"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"For a full alpha-dependency regression, additionally copy the repository's test-only `test`, `tools`"},{"id":"p26s2","text":", `fixtures` directories and the root lockfile into that unpacked package and run `node --test` from"},{"id":"p26s3","text":" it. These fixtures are intentionally not distributed in the npm tarball."},{"id":"p27s1","text":"## 0.1.31: merged `main`, native rootless media fetch"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"## 0.1.29: reproducible repository release"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"Runtime behavior is unchanged from the phone- and desktop-accepted 0.1.28. This release synchronizes"},{"id":"p30s2","text":" the verified source, dependency lock and offline native-client contract fixtures into Git. The pinn"},{"id":"p30s3","text":"ed third-party fixtures are test-only and excluded from the npm package."},{"id":"p31s1","text":"## 0.1.28: busy enqueue confirmation"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
